  },
  "note": "Annual election of one third (five seats), Thursday 15 January 1914, for the places of Dr J. M. Moore, Edward Lunn, James Gillespie, Henry Megarry and William Miller. Eight were nominated, but Robert Duke had told the electors he was not seeking election and had failed, through a misunderstanding, to lodge his withdrawal, so the contest lay between seven. \"The poll was the smallest for several years, only 1,658 out of a register of 2,424 exercising the franchise.\" Declared at 10.30 p.m. The spoiled papers are not given. No party labels printed."
